WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.790
It's a great time to be a sci-fi fan, but
which films should you be watching?

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.070
The past year gave us an onslaught of mind-bending
adventures to choose from.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:14.269
So without further ado, here are the best
sci-fi movies of 2020.

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:19.561
Canadian auteur filmmaker David Cronenberg
has masterfully merged horror and sci-fi themes

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:24.470
on numerous occasions throughout his career,
and his son, Brandon Cronenberg, managed the

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.849
same feat with 2020's Possessor.

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:31.199
The film was met with rave reviews, earning
widespread praise from the critics.

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:35.829
Possessor is the story of Tasya - played by
Mandy's Andrea Riseborough, an agent of a

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:39.920
corporation that uses brain-implant tech to
take control of people.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.100
Victims are turned into unwilling hitmen,
carrying out assassinations ordered by the

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.270
company's rich and powerful clients.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:50.920
Tasya is a natural at the job, but she gets
more than she bargained for when she inhabits

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.780
the body of a man whose thirst for violence
eclipses even her own.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.350
The experienced agent loses control of her
host's mind and finds herself in danger of

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.989
never being able to escape it, leading to
a thrilling (and highly abstract) showdown

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:06.330
between possessor and host.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.210
“Pull me out.”

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:15.000
If any one movie was going to coax people
back into theaters in 2020, it was Tenet.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.220
Christopher Nolan's eleventh feature was the
first blockbuster to play in theaters during

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.698
the coronavirus pandemic, and it certainly
helped people take their minds off COVID-19 for a while.

00:01:24.698 --> 00:01:30.509
John David Washington stars as a former CIA
agent who's been recruited by a secret organization,

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:33.710
Tenet, which is working to prevent World War
III.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:38.520
He learns that weapons with "inverted entropy"
manufactured in the future are somehow making

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.420
their way to the present day, and things get
a whole lot weirder from there.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.939
With help from Robert Pattinson's Neil, Washington's
unnamed protagonist learns that a Russian

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:49.470
oligarch has been in contact with the future.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:53.590
Our descendants have grown tired of the ravaged
world left to them, and they intend to invert

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.869
the flow of time in a last ditch effort to
change the world.

00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:01.790
It may not be Christopher Nolan's finest film,
but the slick action sequences and impeccable

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:06.160
performances make Tenet one of 2020's must-see
sci-fi films.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:11.280
If an homage to Ridley Scott's Alien set during
the height of the Cold War sounds like something

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.290
you'd be interested in, you need to check
out Sputnik.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.290
This slick Russian creature feature was forced
to forgo a theatrical release because of the

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:23.070
coronavirus pandemic, but it found lots of
love on VOD in its native country.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:28.319
Genre film distributor IFC Midnight secured
the release rights for North America, where

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:31.870
critics have been raving about Egor Abramenko's
stylish debut.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:37.970
On paper, Abramenko's story is nothing groundbreaking,
but he executes his scary alien vision superbly.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:43.420
Sputnik follows a cosmonaut who gets quarantined
after his vessel malfunctions reentering the

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.420
Earth's atmosphere.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:48.800
What he doesn't know is that there's an extraterrestrial
parasite living inside him, and when he sleeps,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.989
it comes out to feed.

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:54.099
The Russian military manages to keep this
a secret, hoping to separate the creature

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:56.810
from its host and use it as a weapon of war.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:02.168
The cosmonaut's only hope is a sympathetic
neurophysiologist, who begins masterminding his escape.

00:03:02.168 --> 00:03:07.185
With suspense to spare, Sputnik is a white-knuckle
thrill ride that you can't afford to miss.

00:03:07.185 --> 00:03:12.290
Sci-fi comedy Save Yourselves! is the story
of a young Brooklyn couple who decide to disconnect

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.900
from the modern world for a while.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.930
They head out into rural New York without
their phones or devices.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:21.830
While they're away, aliens invade Earth, and
our heroes have absolutely no idea.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:26.580
As cities across America are reduced to rubble,
our heroes busy themselves with un-busying

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:27.580
themselves.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:31.860
The city-dwellers take advantage of the nearby
lake and surrounding nature, blissfully unaware

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.210
that humankind is under attack from fluffy
(but extremely vicious) extraterrestrials.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:41.600
Gradually, they come to the realization that
something isn't quite right, and their Millennial

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.080
morals are tested when they discover a gun
in the cabin's basement.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.641
When push comes to shove, they would rather
bear arms than be killed by a ball of space fluff.

00:03:49.641 --> 00:03:54.800
Writer/directors Alex Huston Fischer and Eleanor
Wilson didn't have a huge budget, so the majority

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.920
of the action – including the leveling of
Yankee Stadium – happens off-screen.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.310
This isn't a big, VFX-heavy sci-fi film, but
it really doesn't need to be.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.870
Sunita Mani and John Paul Reynolds are both
funny and convincing as Su and Jack, and their

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:13.140
vacation-turned-survival mission is engaging
enough that we don't need to see all the peripheral destruction.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:16.090
“We need to turn our phones back on!”

00:04:18.735 --> 00:04:19.907
“Sorry, making a smoothie.

00:04:19.907 --> 00:04:22.828
Listen… it’s getting weird here in New
York!”

00:04:22.976 --> 00:04:27.139
Bill &amp; Ted Face the Music was a tonic for
trying times in 2020.

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:31.790
Alex Winter's Bill S. Preston, Esquire and
Keanu Reeves' Ted Theodore Logan returned

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:36.360
to the big screen for a belated third adventure
in late summer, though the coronavirus pandemic

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.790
meant it had an unusual theatrical release.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:44.120
Box office returns were a predictably dire
$3.3 million, but Bill &amp; Ted Face the Music

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:49.550
was also released on PVOD, and Deadline sources
suggest it made around ten times that amount

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.300
via streaming in the same period.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.910
The simultaneous release meant critics nationwide
got to see the movie, and the majority of

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.750
them deemed it most excellent.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.340
Our titular besties are now middle-aged fathers.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.320
As Bill and Ted go forward in time in search
of their future selves, their daughters go

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:08.260
in the opposite direction, recruiting iconic
musicians for the band that will help their

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.330
dads finally perform their universe-saving
song.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.000
Reeves and Winter slip back into their roles
with ease, and their onscreen daughters are

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.150
just as watchable.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:20.680
Variety called the film "a blissed-out air
balloon of nostalgia" in a glowing review,

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:25.807
while The Hollywood Reporter called it, quote,
"almost exactly as good as its two big-screen predecessors."

00:05:26.274 --> 00:05:31.570
Archive may not win any awards for originality,
but as The Hollywood Reporter put it, the

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:36.270
directorial debut of concept artist Gavin
Rothery is a, quote, "sleek and satisfying

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.479
riff on familiar sci-fi themes."

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:44.169
Rothery’s film plays like a mash-up of Ex-Machina
and Black Mirror, and takes place in 2038,

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:49.060
when a widowed roboticist named George Almore
is on the verge of a groundbreaking advancement.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:52.979
Almore works for a megacorporation that specializes
in artificial intelligence.

00:05:52.979 --> 00:05:57.861
When we meet him, his human-equivalent prototype
is just about ready, but this isn't just a

00:05:57.861 --> 00:06:04.100
replication of any old human - the savvy scientist
has recreated his deceased wife in robot AI

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.699
form behind the backs of his bosses.

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:08.949
The trouble is, his creation ends up being
a little too real.

00:06:08.949 --> 00:06:13.150
We're not going to spoil it here, but trust
us when we say that Archive contains one of

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:16.990
the best movie twists of 2020, sci-fi or otherwise.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:22.980
Sci-fi adventure Love and Monsters proved
popular when it was released on PVOD in October

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.180
2020, and the critics loved it too.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:29.750
This dystopian teen film takes place some
seven years after mankind turned its nukes

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:33.330
on a planet-killing asteroid that was on a
collision course with Earth.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:38.160
They destroyed their intended target, but
nobody was quite prepared for the brutal aftermath:

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:43.040
the fallout caused all cold-blooded animals
to mutate into huge, terrifying creatures.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:47.520
Former Maze Runner star Dylan O'Brien leads
the line as one of a number of survivors living

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:48.840
in an underground bunker.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:54.099
The film was lauded as an "imaginative post-apocalyptic
coming-of-age film" by the New York Times,

00:06:54.099 --> 00:06:58.639
while Variety called it a, quote, "daffily
lightweight throwback to the teen action-adventures

00:06:58.639 --> 00:07:00.259
of the '80s and '90s."

00:07:00.259 --> 00:07:04.580
Marvel fans will recognize some familiar faces
here - Joel's girlfriend Aimee is played by

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.610
Iron Fist star Jessica Henwick.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:10.919
Michael Rooker of Guardians of the Galaxy
and Ariana Greenblatt from Avengers: Infinity

00:07:10.919 --> 00:07:13.804
War also make appearances in the film..

00:07:13.804 --> 00:07:19.620
Spontaneous was one of the most critically-acclaimed
movies of 2020, scoring a near-perfect 98

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.180
percent on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:26.259
In Brian Duffield's directorial debut, students
at Covington High School have started to inexplicably

00:07:26.259 --> 00:07:31.340
explode at random intervals, sowing dread
and anxiety among their surviving classmates.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:36.069
The film's quarantine scenes drew inevitable
comparisons to the coronavirus pandemic, but

00:07:36.069 --> 00:07:40.009
Spontaneous was done and dusted before COVID-19
was a thing.

00:07:40.009 --> 00:07:43.610
According to Duffield, his goal was to make
a movie that captured what it meant to be

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:45.540
a kid at that moment in time.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.580
He said, in his Looper exclusive interview:

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.979
"I'm very liberal, and for me, the movie feels
like a very real thing that kids are dealing

00:07:51.979 --> 00:07:53.169
with right now.

00:07:53.169 --> 00:07:56.720
When we shot the movie, there were these things
happening in the world where it really felt

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.500
like kids were being like, 'We need someone
to help us.'

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.349
And it was really falling on deaf ears."

00:08:01.349 --> 00:08:05.789
The writer-director also revealed that '80s
classic Heathers and the films of John Hughes

00:08:05.789 --> 00:08:07.994
were among his many inspirations.

00:08:07.994 --> 00:08:13.040
Fifty Shades of Gray star Jamie Dornan and
Avengers actor Anthony Mackie play a pair

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.830
of paramedics in Synchronic, a New Orleans-set
sci-fi that made a big impression when it

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.039
premiered at the Toronto International Film
Festival.

00:08:21.039 --> 00:08:25.530
Directed by Justin Benson and Aaron Moorhead,
Synchronic follows Dennis and Steve as they're

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:28.000
called to a series of strange and gruesome
incidents.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:31.949
The pair believes that a new designer drug
called “synchronic” is to blame for it

00:08:31.949 --> 00:08:37.054
all, but when Dennis' daughter mysteriously
goes missing, it's up to Steve to investigate further.

00:08:37.054 --> 00:08:41.039
He soon discovers that synchronic is more
than meets the eye - these mysterious pills

00:08:41.039 --> 00:08:43.400
allow the user to travel through time.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:47.440
One of the many criticisms leveled at the
Fifty Shades franchise was that the co-stars

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.860
had zero chemistry, but that certainly isn't
a problem here.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:54.970
Dornan and Mackie sell their relationship
well, delivering believable performances as

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.382
two best friends going through personal ruts.

00:08:57.382 --> 00:09:02.036
Synchronic gets pretty trippy, but the two
leads keep us invested in their modern day problems.

